# Real-Time Object Detection on ZedBoard — Vitis HLS Approach

## PYNQ+FINN vs Vitis HLS Comparison

| Aspect | PYNQ + FINN | **Vitis HLS** ✅ |
|--------|-------------|-------------------|
| Language | Python only | **C/C++ → Hardware** |
| Control | Limited (black-box) | **Full control over architecture** |
| Learning | Low | **High — understand HW/SW co-design** |
| Novelty Score | Low (auto-generated) | **High — custom accelerator** |
| Competition Edge | Weak | **Strong — shows deep understanding** |
| Difficulty | Easy | Moderate (we'll simplify it) |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Vitis HLS lets you write C++ that gets automatically compiled into FPGA hardware.** You don't need to write Verilog. The tool handles the translation to RTL.

---

## System Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph HOST["Laptop"]
        CAM[Webcam Capture]
        DISP[Display Results]
    end

    subgraph PS["ARM Cortex-A9 (PS)"]
        DRV[DMA Driver]
        PRE[Preprocess<br/>Resize + Normalize]
        POST[Postprocess<br/>NMS + Bounding Boxes]
    end

    subgraph PL["FPGA Fabric (PL)"]
        direction TB
        DMA_IN[AXI DMA In]
        CONV1[Conv2D Layer 1<br/>HLS IP]
        RELU1[ReLU]
        POOL1[MaxPool]
        CONV2[Conv2D Layer 2<br/>HLS IP]
        RELU2[ReLU]
        POOL2[MaxPool]
        FC[Fully Connected<br/>HLS IP]
        DMA_OUT[AXI DMA Out]
        
        DMA_IN --> CONV1 --> RELU1 --> POOL1
        POOL1 --> CONV2 --> RELU2 --> POOL2
        POOL2 --> FC --> DMA_OUT
    end

    CAM -->|Ethernet| PRE
    PRE -->|AXI DMA| DMA_IN
    DMA_OUT -->|AXI DMA| POST
    POST -->|Ethernet| DISP
```

### Data Flow

```
Laptop Camera → [Ethernet] → ARM (preprocess) → [AXI DMA] → FPGA Accelerator → [AXI DMA] → ARM (postprocess) → [Ethernet] → Laptop Display
```

