## Phase 5: CPU-Only Baseline

Implement the **exact same CNN** in pure C on the ARM core without FPGA — for comparison.

```c
// cpu_inference.c — No FPGA, pure ARM
void cpu_conv2d(float input[], float weights[], float output[]) {
    // Same convolution but running on ARM CPU
    // No HLS pragmas, no DMA — just software loops
    for (int oc = 0; oc < OUT_CH; oc++)
        for (int oh = 0; oh < OUT_H; oh++)
            for (int ow = 0; ow < OUT_W; ow++) {
                float sum = 0;
                for (int ic = 0; ic < IN_CH; ic++)
                    for (int kh = 0; kh < K; kh++)
                        for (int kw = 0; kw < K; kw++)
                            sum += input[ic][oh+kh][ow+kw] 
                                 * weights[oc][ic][kh][kw];
                output[oc][oh][ow] = (sum > 0) ? sum : 0; // ReLU
            }
}
```

